I would give them a big goose egg if I could. We pulled in with our travel trailer and NO ONE came out of the bldg, house or trailer for about 15 min. My husband had to walk around the bldg for a good 15 min before he finally caught someone's attention. A man came out of a trailer that was on the property--NOT the 'Pastor'--just some guy staying on the property. My husband talked to him for about 5 min and then behold the 'Pastor' emerged! Not friendly, more  like we interrupted his nap. My husband explained that we are on our way  out of state and due to unforseen circumstances --including COVID economy --we are traveling on God's mercy and grace, town by town, mile by mile. We are selling, bartering and trading what we have for what we need. Someone recommended this place and said that you would help. All we needed was some water and/or gas? We got shot down and his answer made my jaw drop: "NO....services are closed for the season; and when we do help it is only 2 or 3 days a week, maybe. We don't have homeless here now." I'm thinking: What? Did they just disappear or did you push them away as you are us??? People need help all year round; NOT just "in season" -- dude. He explained that the Pre-Covid Pastor was the one who helped people, but he has since passed away. Ohhh, I get it, your the new one and you stopped helping people. I imagine he is rolling in his grave about how his church is now. Couldn't even let us have some water!!! Soooo..if you are ever heading to Quartzsite bring extra of what you need because there is no help in this place, esp  off-season. Can you say unfriendly ghost town?? Maybe it's the heat.
Posted: KF of {TNT}
Score: Tried-N-Flunked
